### Enterprise Domain Architecture: Employee Hierarchy

In this guided capstone project, you combine every inheritance concept learned throughout this module into a production-grade corporate employee management system:

* **Superclass `Employee`**: Centralizes common attributes (`id`, `name`, `baseSalary`) and business methods (`calculateMonthlyPay()`, `printBadge()`).
* **Subclass `SoftwareEngineer extends Employee`**: Specializes `Employee` by adding programming language expertise, bug bounty bonuses, and code review workflows.
* **Subclass `EngineeringManager extends Employee`**: Specializes `Employee` by adding team size tracking, quarterly management stipends, and team synchronization meetings.
* **Subclass `TechnicalDirector extends EngineeringManager`**: Demonstrates **multilevel inheritance** (`Employee` &rarr; `Manager` &rarr; `Director`), adding stock options and departmental budget approvals!

---

### Complete Runnable Implementation

Here is the complete, runnable enterprise system:

```java
// 1. Root Superclass
class Employee {
    protected String employeeId;
    protected String fullName;
    protected double baseSalary;

    public Employee(String id, String name, double salary) {
        this.employeeId = id;
        this.fullName = name;
        this.baseSalary = salary;
    }

    public double calculateMonthlyPay() {
        return baseSalary / 12.0;
    }

    public void printRosterEntry() {
        System.out.printf("[%s] %-18s | Monthly Base: $%.2f%n", employeeId, fullName, calculateMonthlyPay());
    }
}

// 2. Specialized Subclass: SoftwareEngineer
class SoftwareEngineer extends Employee {
    private String primaryLanguage;
    private double monthlyBonus;

    public SoftwareEngineer(String id, String name, double salary, String language, double bonus) {
        super(id, name, salary);
        this.primaryLanguage = language;
        this.monthlyBonus = bonus;
    }

    @Override
    public double calculateMonthlyPay() {
        return super.calculateMonthlyPay() + monthlyBonus;
    }

    @Override
    public void printRosterEntry() {
        System.out.printf("[%s] %-18s | Total: $%.2f (Dev: %s + $%.0f bonus)%n",
                employeeId, fullName, calculateMonthlyPay(), primaryLanguage, monthlyBonus);
    }
}

// 3. Specialized Subclass: EngineeringManager
class EngineeringManager extends Employee {
    protected int directReports;
    protected double leadershipStipend;

    public EngineeringManager(String id, String name, double salary, int reports, double stipend) {
        super(id, name, salary);
        this.directReports = reports;
        this.leadershipStipend = stipend;
    }

    @Override
    public double calculateMonthlyPay() {
        return super.calculateMonthlyPay() + leadershipStipend;
    }

    @Override
    public void printRosterEntry() {
        System.out.printf("[%s] %-18s | Total: $%.2f (Manager: %d reports)%n",
                employeeId, fullName, calculateMonthlyPay(), directReports);
    }
}

// 4. Multilevel Subclass: TechnicalDirector extends EngineeringManager
class TechnicalDirector extends EngineeringManager {
    private int equityShares;

    public TechnicalDirector(String id, String name, double salary, int reports, double stipend, int shares) {
        super(id, name, salary, reports, stipend);
        this.equityShares = shares;
    }

    @Override
    public void printRosterEntry() {
        System.out.printf("[%s] %-18s | Total: $%.2f (Director: %d reports, %d equity units)%n",
                employeeId, fullName, calculateMonthlyPay(), directReports, equityShares);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("=========================================================================");
        System.out.println("                 ENTERPRISE GLOBAL ROSTER REPORT                         ");
        System.out.println("=========================================================================");

        Employee dev = new SoftwareEngineer("EMP-101", "Marcus Vance", 120000.0, "Java/Spring", 1200.0);
        Employee mgr = new EngineeringManager("EMP-204", "Sarah Lin", 150000.0, 8, 2500.0);
        Employee dir = new TechnicalDirector("EMP-309", "David Chen", 210000.0, 45, 5000.0, 10000);

        dev.printRosterEntry();
        mgr.printRosterEntry();
        dir.printRosterEntry();

        System.out.println("=========================================================================");
    }
}
```

**Console Output:**
```text
=========================================================================
                 ENTERPRISE GLOBAL ROSTER REPORT                         
=========================================================================
[EMP-101] Marcus Vance       | Total: $11200.00 (Dev: Java/Spring + $1200 bonus)
[EMP-204] Sarah Lin          | Total: $15000.00 (Manager: 8 reports)
[EMP-309] David Chen         | Total: $22500.00 (Director: 45 reports, 10000 equity units)
=========================================================================
```

---

### Architectural Highlights Demonstrated

This project validates all core Java OOP principles in a real-world design:
* **The extends Keyword**: Links each specialized role to its base entity with zero duplicated field definitions.
* **Constructor Chaining**: `super(...)` delegates state initialization up the hierarchy safely.
* **Multilevel Inheritance**: `TechnicalDirector` extends `EngineeringManager`, automatically inheriting both `Employee` and `Manager` capabilities.
* **Clean Code & Encapsulation**: Private fields protect specialized attributes, while protected members enable smooth inheritance.

